<!-- EXPANDING SECTORS -->
<section class="target-sectors" id="target">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="target-intro reveal">
      <div class="section-tag"><div class="line"></div><span>Where We Are Growing</span></div>
      <h2 class="section-headline">Equipment Ready.<br>Experience Transferable.</h2>
      <p>The equipment we build for cement plants, mines, and food processing operations is the same equipment these sectors need — the material characteristics differ, the engineering principles do not. If your operation in any of these sectors handles bulk solids, powders, or granular material, Jayveecons has fabricated something like it before.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="target-grid">

      <div class="target-card reveal">
        <svg class="tc-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v16a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/><polyline points="10 9 9 9 8 9"/></svg>
        <div class="tc-name">Oil &amp; Gas</div>
        <div class="tc-status">Diversifying With Proven Equipment</div>
        <p class="tc-desc">Upstream and midstream oil and gas operations move large volumes of bulk solids — proppants (frac sand), drilling muds, barite, and bentonite in drilling; petroleum coke, catalyst fines, and sulphur in refining. These materials demand enclosed, leak-proof conveying systems and pressure-rated containment vessels built to material-specific standards.</p>
        <div class="tc-opportunity">
          <strong>What we bring to this sector:</strong> Enclosed screw conveyors suited to dusty and hazardous bulk solids; belt and bucket systems scaled for high-volume proppant handling at drilling sites; fabricated pressure vessels and storage systems for bulk chemical intermediates; experience with abrasion-resistant material selection from our mining work. Where API or ASME documentation is specified, we work to those requirements.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="target-card reveal">
        <svg class="tc-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M9 3H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v4m6-6h10a2 2 0 012 2v4M9 3v18m0 0h10a2 2 0 002-2V9M9 21H5a2 2 0 01-2-2V9m0 0h18"/></svg>
        <div class="tc-name">Pharmaceuticals</div>
        <div class="tc-status">Diversifying With Proven Equipment</div>
        <p class="tc-desc">Pharmaceutical bulk handling requires precision, containment, and cleanability above all else. Active pharmaceutical ingredients (APIs), excipients, and formulation powders must be transferred without contamination, without cross-mixing, and with full material traceability. Equipment construction must permit clean-in-place or strip-down cleaning, with no crevices, dead zones, or surface finishes that trap product.</p>
        <div class="tc-opportunity">
          <strong>What we bring to this sector:</strong> Stainless steel screw conveyors and bucket elevators designed to Ra surface finish requirements; crevice-free weld geometry; contained transfer points that eliminate open-air product exposure; IBC handling systems; full material certification (mill certificates, test reports) and dimensional inspection documentation. Our food-grade fabrication experience is the direct foundation for pharma-grade work.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="target-card reveal">
        <svg class="tc-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M12 2a10 10 0 100 20A10 10 0 0012 2z"/><path d="M12 6v6l4 2"/><path d="M2 12h4M18 12h4M12 6V2M12 22v-4"/></svg>
        <div class="tc-name">Agriculture Processing</div>
        <div class="tc-status">Diversifying With Proven Equipment</div>
        <p class="tc-desc">Industrial-scale post-harvest operations — grain reception and storage, oilseed crushing, rice milling, sugar processing, and animal feed compounding — require handling systems that are high-throughput, gentle on product quality, and designed for the seasonal intensity of harvest intake. Moisture management, pest exclusion, and dust control are critical operating parameters, not afterthoughts.</p>
        <div class="tc-opportunity">
          <strong>What we bring to this sector:</strong> High-capacity bucket elevators and belt conveyors for grain intake and transfer; flat-bottom and hopper-bottom silos for short and long-term storage with aeration systems; rotary dryers for moisture reduction of harvested grain; screw conveyors and feeders for milling and blending operations. Our food-processing background means food-safe material selection is standard, not an upgrade.
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
